analysisWe need to produce an assert statement for the comment after clone method.

Comment: "@@@ For every valid index in the original list, the element at that index in the cloned list is the same as the element at that index in the original list."

We need to express: For all int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size() (original list size) => cloned list's element at i equals original's element at i.

But we need to refer to the result of the method: the cloned list is returned, stored in \result. Use observer methods: we have get(int index) method to retrieve element at index. So we can write: \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); \result.get(i).equals(this.get(i))

Need to consider null elements: equals may be null safe? In Java, we could use Objects.equals, but they use .equals. In spec examples they used .equals for objects. For null, .equals would throw NPE, but spec may assume elements non-null or we can use \result.get(i) == this.get(i) or Objects.equals. We can use \result.get(i).equals(\old(...))? No old not needed because we compare original before cloning. The original list hasn't changed. So we can just use this.get(i). Use \result.get(i).equals(this.get(i)). That's fine.

Thus final assert: assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); \result.get(i).equals(this.get(i));

